The bundled Chulapa font requires no external loading. To use it on headings, you must first set `headings-font-family: "chulapa, sans-serif"` under `chulapa-skin.vars`. Simply using ligature CSS alone does not select the font. For heading ligatures, you must use `assets/css/custom.scss` with an empty YAML front matter:

```scss
---
---
h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
  font-feature-settings: "liga", "dlig";
  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
}
```

Regarding Cactus comments, the context does not contain information about whether configuring Cactus loads the Chulapa font on every page.

Sources:
* [Bundled font](https://dieghernan.github.io/chulapa/docs/53-chulapa-font)
* [Cactus comments](https://dieghernan.github.io/chulapa/docs/39-cactus-comments)
